      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Examples of the dynamic bone setup used for the avatar vs what happens when it gets converted to physbones without changing the root. This is of course easily fixed by adding a root bone for the hair, this is just to show what's going on in-game essentially.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-08T02:42:12.854Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With Dynamic Bones, the root bone is not counted in the chain of bones, whereas with Physbones, the root bone is counted. This causes issues with auto conversion of some avatars, such as if an avatar uses the head of the avatar as the root bone.\nThis unfortunately breaks a *lot* of avatars and it'd probably be best to add an exception for avatars that are automatically converted in-game for the root bone in these cases to avoid issues.\nA video of the problem in-action causing the head to rotate improperly:\nhttps://youtu.be/3FlLmhZdNjE\n\nTurning off the automatic conversion does work as a workaround but it's not ideal.",
